{"kind":"table","sheet":"Template","address":"A1:E27","rows":27,"cols":5,"values":[["It is recommended that you do not edit rubrics in spreadsheet format",null,null,null,null],["v1.0-s",null,null,null,null],["Four-slide structure, title, and student name",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: (1) uses the presentation template in Google Classroom; (2) includes exactly four slides; (3) Slide 1 has a clear title about ultrasonic sensors; and (4) Slide 1 includes the student's full name.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,2,0],[null,"Exceeds Standard","Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Not Yet Demonstrated"],[null,"4 pts = all 4 checks are complete.","3 pts = 3 checks are complete.","2 pts = 2 checks are complete.","0 pts = 0–1 check is complete or no presentation is submitted."],["What is an ultrasonic sensor?",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: explains that an ultrasonic sensor (1) measures distance; (2) sends a high-frequency sound pulse; (3) listens for the returning echo; and (4) uses the echo's travel time to determine distance.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,2,0],[null,"Exceeds Standard","Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Not Yet Demonstrated"],[null,"4 pts = all 4 ideas are accurate and clear.","3 pts = 3 ideas are accurate and clear.","2 pts = 2 ideas are accurate and clear.","0 pts = 0–1 idea is accurate, or the explanation is missing."],["Parts of the ultrasonic sensor",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: correctly identifies and explains (1) VCC/power; (2) GND/ground; (3) TRIG and the transmitting element that sends the pulse; and (4) ECHO and the receiving element that detects the return. Labels or a clear diagram may be used.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,2,0],[null,"Exceeds Standard","Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Not Yet Demonstrated"],[null,"4 pts = all 4 parts or part-groups are correctly identified and explained.","3 pts = 3 parts or part-groups are correctly identified and explained.","2 pts = 2 parts or part-groups are correctly identified and explained.","0 pts = 0–1 part or part-group is correct, or the parts slide is missing."],["Sensor connection and data collection",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: using the teacher-provided code, the student (1) connects VCC and GND correctly; (2) connects TRIG and ECHO to the assigned pins; (3) keeps the circuit safe, powered correctly, and organized; and (4) obtains stable readings at different object distances. Writing the code is not assessed.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,2,0],[null,"Exceeds Standard","Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Not Yet Demonstrated"],[null,"4 pts = all 4 connection and collection checks are demonstrated.","3 pts = 3 checks are demonstrated; minor help or correction is needed.","2 pts = 2 checks are demonstrated; repeated help or correction is needed.","0 pts = 0–1 check is demonstrated, the sensor is not connected, or no readings are obtained."],["Five distance readings and a reliable near/far threshold",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: Slide 4 (1) records at least 5 actual distance readings; (2) gives the unit for every reading; (3) states one numerical threshold and clearly defines which values are Near and which are Far; and (4) uses the collected readings or repeated tests to explain why the threshold is reliable.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,2,0],[null,"Exceeds Standard","Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Not Yet Demonstrated"],[null,"4 pts = all 4 data and threshold checks are complete, including at least 5 readings.","3 pts = at least 5 readings are recorded and 3 checks are complete.","2 pts = only 3–4 readings are recorded, or only 2 checks are complete.","0 pts = 0–2 readings are recorded, no numerical threshold is given, or Slide 4 is missing."]]}
